# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets out of it.
#
# `.env` is the one that matters: the image is built with NEXT_PUBLIC_* passed as build
# arguments, and everything else is supplied at run time by docker-compose. A `.env` copied
# into a layer would sit in the image history whether or not anything read it.

node_modules
.next
.git
.gitignore

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml

npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
